gametitle=Champions: Return to Arms (SLUS-20973) v2.00

// fp-proposed.pnach - a PROPOSAL, not part of the fix set (patches/SLUS-20973_4028A55F.pnach) and not in
// tools/play-net/sections-suggested.txt.  docs/issues/native-first-person-controls.md 2.6 says what it is for,
// what was run with it and what it would mean to adopt it: every player of a game needs the same set of
// sections, so this becomes real only as a section of the fix set that everybody has.
// Written by local/recomp-fp-controls/work/fpasm.py (kept beside the tests; the words below are its output).

[Proposed: strafe mode - a player can run one way and face another]
author=first-person controls work, 2026-10-13; run on the native build only (one copy, and two copies in one lockstep game); untested on the emulator build, PCSX2 or a console
description=The game runs a character along its facing and turns the facing to the stick: there is no way to run sideways or backwards while facing ahead, which a view from the character's eyes wants. With this section each player has a mode byte (player object +0x47E, a byte that only the unreachable jump state used). While it is 0 the game is exactly as it was. While it is not 0, in the ordinary moving state the character turns (40 % of the angle a tick, the game's own rate) to where the camera of its player looks - the heading a pushed-up stick asks for, 0x3E3D minus the yaw word that already travels with every controller row - and runs along the stick's own direction instead of along its facing, at the same speed. The mode is set by game message 4, sub-type 2 {2, slot, mode}: message 4 already exists, travels in lockstep and has an empty handler; every machine sets the byte in the same tick. Player_ctor now clears the byte, so every new character (level start, respawn) starts with the mode off on every machine. Four parts: the hook in Player_move (0x1B4210), its code in the unreferenced function 0x2128C8, the handler and a sender in the unreferenced function 0x215C98 (the sender is called with the mode in a0, at 0x215CDC), the jump from the empty handler 0x1E01B0, and the two byte stores of the constructor. Every player must have this section or none.
// Player_move 0x1b4210; was: 24020005 12A2007C
// j 0x2128c8
patch=1,EE,001B4210,word,08084A32
// addiu v0,zero,0x5
patch=1,EE,001B4214,word,24020005
// Player_ctor 0x1a22fc; was: A2A0047C A2A0047D
// sh zero,0x47c(s5)
patch=1,EE,001A22FC,word,A6A0047C
// sb zero,0x47e(s5)
patch=1,EE,001A2300,word,A2A0047E
// the empty handler of game message 4, 0x1e01b0; was: 03E00008 00000000
